---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const EMAIL = 'hello@hamzatekin.dev';
// Update both after each accessibility review.
const reviewed = { iso: '2026-10-10', label: '10 October 2026' };
---

<Layout
  title="Accessibility statement - Hamza Tekin"
  description="How accessible hamzatekin.dev is, how it was tested against WCAG 2.2 AA, and how to report a problem."
>
  <article class="prose-page mb-24">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">Accessibility statement</h1>
    <p class="text-sm">Last reviewed <time datetime={reviewed.iso}>{reviewed.label}</time></p>

    <p>
      I want everyone to be able to use this site, including people who use a screen reader, screen magnification, voice control or a
      keyboard instead of a mouse. This statement covers every page on hamzatekin.dev.
    </p>

    <h2 id="status">Conformance status</h2>
    <p>
      This site fully conforms to the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</a> at level AA.
      Fully conforms means every page meets all level A and AA success criteria, with no exceptions.
    </p>
    <p>
      WCAG 2.2 AA is also the web requirement in EN 301 549 v4.1.1, the European standard for accessible ICT used with the European
      Accessibility Act. This is a personal website, so neither that Act nor the UK's public sector accessibility regulations apply to it,
      but I hold it to the same standard.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what-you-can-do">What you can do on this site</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Zoom in to 400% without having to scroll sideways.</li>
      <li>Change text size, spacing, fonts and colours with your browser settings or extensions without losing content.</li>
      <li>Reach every link and control with a keyboard, with a clearly visible focus outline.</li>
      <li>Find your way with a screen reader using headings, landmarks and link text that makes sense on its own.</li>
      <li>Know in advance which links open a new tab, because screen readers announce it.</li>
      <li>Turn off motion. Page transitions stop when your device is set to reduce motion.</li>
      <li>
        Get more contrast. Secondary text and borders get brighter when your device asks for more contrast, and the layout works with
        Windows contrast themes.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use the site without JavaScript. The only feature that needs it is the analytics switch on the <a href="/privacy#turn-off"
          >privacy page</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="testing">How I tested</h2>
    <p>The site was last tested on <time datetime={reviewed.iso}>{reviewed.label}</time>, with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>automated checks with axe-core against the WCAG 2.2 A and AA rules, on every page, at desktop width and at 320 pixels wide</li>
      <li>keyboard-only navigation through every page, checking focus order and focus visibility</li>
      <li>reflow at 320 CSS pixels wide, the same as 400% zoom on a 1280 pixel screen, with and without WCAG's text spacing overrides</li>
      <li>Windows contrast themes, reduced motion and increased contrast, emulated in Chromium</li>
      <li>contrast ratios measured for every text and focus colour against its background</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="limitations">Known limitations</h2>
    <p>
      I do not know of any accessibility problems on this site. If you find one, please tell me. Links to GitHub, LinkedIn and npm go to
      sites I do not control, and their accessibility may differ.
    </p>

    <h2 id="compatibility">Compatibility</h2>
    <p>
      The site is plain HTML and CSS. It is built to work in current versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari, and with screen readers
      such as VoiceOver, NVDA, JAWS and TalkBack.
    </p>

    <h2 id="feedback">Feedback and contact</h2>
    <p>
      If something on this site does not work for you, or you need any of it in a different format, email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}
        >{EMAIL}</a
      >. Tell me which page you were on and what went wrong. I will reply within 5 working days.
    </p>

    <h2 id="enforcement">If you are not happy with my response</h2>
    <p>
      In the UK, the <a href="https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com/">Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS)</a> gives free advice on
      discrimination, including services that are not accessible.
    </p>

    <h2 id="preparation">Preparation of this statement</h2>
    <p>
      I wrote this statement on <time datetime="2026-10-10">10 October 2026</time> and last reviewed it on <time datetime={reviewed.iso}
        >{reviewed.label}</time
      >. I review it whenever the site changes in a way that could affect accessibility.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
